   {
    "day": 0,
    "k": "arthur",
    "ans": "On Monday, to pay the rent; Tuesday, to get himself a pair of boots; Wednesday, to take Joan to see her grandparents in Peckham; Thursday, to buy fish for Friday; Friday, to post his weekly balance-sheet to head-quarters; and Saturday, to wash and dress himself, and go to church.",
    "items": 0
   },
   {
    "day": 0,
    "k": "arthur",
    "ans": "On Tuesday, he would post his books, set his room to rights, and go to see his mother. On Wednesday, he would wash and mend his clothes, and read. On Thursday, he would take Joan to see her grandmother. On Friday, he would cash his wages, and pay the bills. On Saturday, he would clean himself, and go to walk.",
    "items": 5
   },
   {
    "day": 0,
    "k": "thomas",
    "ans": "On Tuesday he would see to the insurance of his furniture, and correct his balance-sheet. On Wednesday he would pay the gas bill. On Thursday he would buy a new hat. On Friday he would pay the tradesmen. On Saturday he would clean his boots.",
    "items": 5
   }
